# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Mizan configuration
#
#   cp .env.example .env      then fill in the two Supabase values
#
# ── How this file reaches the app ──────────────────────────────
# It is NOT bundled. `.env` is deliberately not a Flutter asset: anything in
# pubspec.yaml's asset list is a file inside the APK, so `unzip -p app.apk
# assets/flutter_assets/.env` would print every key in it, and a web build would
# serve it at /assets/.env. It used to be listed, and v1.0.0 shipped that way.
#
# Values now arrive as compile-time constants instead:
#
#   tools/run.sh                       development — passes this whole file
#   tools/build_release.sh             release — passes a whitelist, then checks
#                                      the built APK for everything it withheld
#
# Plain `flutter run` also works, but with no values at all: the app starts,
# reading works, and the sign-in screen says it cannot reach the server.
#
# See lib/core/config/build_config.dart for what this protects and what it does
# not. Never commit .env.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Supabase ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Both from: dashboard → Project Settings → API. Required for accounts, Halaqa
# circles and Al-Minbar; everything else in the app works without them.
#
# Must be the hosted project, not a local stack. On a phone 127.0.0.1 is the
# phone, so a localhost URL means account creation fails for everybody you hand
# the APK to — tools/build_release.sh refuses to build a release with one.
#
# These two ARE compiled into the release, on purpose. The anon key names the
# project and carries no privileges of its own: what it can read is decided by
# row-level security policies on the server.
SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_anon_key_here

# ── UmmahAPI ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Quran audio, word-by-word, tafsir, mutashabihat, hadith.
# Optional: every endpoint answers without a key, and a key only lifts the rate
# limit from 5,000/15min to unlimited. Register free at ummahapi.com/register.
# Sent as the X-API-Key header, never in a query string.
#
# Withheld from release builds, because unlike the anon key this one is a real
# secret and a compiled string is still findable with `strings`. So a release
# runs on the anonymous rate limit until the proxy exists.
UMMAH_API_KEY=umh_your_key_here

# ── Groq — Scholar AI ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Read by nothing yet; Scholar AI is not built. Kept here for when it is, and
# withheld from release builds. When it is built the key must live behind a
# proxy, not in the app: a chat key in a client is somebody else's bill.
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_key_here

# ── Feature flags (1 = on, 0 = off; absent = on) ──────────────
# Ship code that is switched off, then flip a flag. These are passed to release
# builds — they decide what the app does and say nothing secret.
FEATURE_HALAQA=1
FEATURE_MINBAR=1
FEATURE_SCHOLAR_AI=1
# Multilingual UI is not implemented; nothing reads this yet.
FEATURE_MULTILINGUAL=0
# Seed a sample circle + Minbar feed on first run. Demos only — leave off.
FEATURE_SEED_SOCIAL=0

# ── Optional overrides, all unset by default ──────────────────
# UMMAH_API_BASE_URL=https://ummahapi.com
#
# A third-party hadith provider, for citations the bundled corpus does not
# carry. Unset means the hadith layer resolves from bundled and cached text and
# says so plainly when a citation has no text yet.
# HADITH_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.com
# HADITH_API_PATH=/hadiths/{collection}/{number}
# HADITH_API_KEY=
# HADITH_API_KEY_HEADER=x-api-key
# HADITH_API_KEY_QUERY=apiKey
